<title>USA: USDA looking at on-farm grain reserve -- Glickman.</title>
<headline>USDA looking at on-farm grain reserve -- Glickman.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department is examining the idea of a new on-farm grain reserve, Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman said Tuesday. But the department has no proposal to give to Congress.</p>
<p>&quot;We're looking at that. We have no proposal in mind,&quot; Glickman said in reply to a question about proposals to reauthorize the Farmer Owned Reserve. Congress eliminated the program, which paid farmers a storage fee, as part of the 1996 farm policy law.</p>
<p>&quot;We've come to no specific legislative solution,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
